{
  "date": "2026-10-14",
  "id": "3723",
  "title": "Maximize Sum of Squares of Digits",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/maximize-sum-of-squares-of-digits/",
  "topics": [
    "Math",
    "Greedy"
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "You are given two positive integers num and sum."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "A positive integer n is good if it satisfies both of the following:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• The number of digits in n is exactly num."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• The sum of digits in n is exactly sum."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "The score of a good integer n is the sum of the squares of digits in n."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Return a string denoting the good integer n that achieves the maximum score. If there are multiple possible integers, return the maximum ​​​​​​​one. If no such integer exists, return an empty string."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Example 1:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Input: num = 2, sum = 3"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Output: \"30\""
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Explanation:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "There are 3 good integers: 12, 21, and 30."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• The score of 12 is 1^2 + 2^2 = 5."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• The score of 21 is 2^2 + 1^2 = 5."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• The score of 30 is 3^2 + 0^2 = 9."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "The maximum score is 9, which is achieved by the good integer 30. Therefore, the answer is \"30\"."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Example 2:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Input: num = 2, sum = 17"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Output: \"98\""
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Explanation:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "There are 2 good integers: 89 and 98."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• The score of 89 is 8^2 + 9^2 = 145."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• The score of 98 is 9^2 + 8^2 = 145."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "The maximum score is 145. The maximum good integer that achieves this score is 98. Therefore, the answer is \"98\"."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Example 3:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Input: num = 1, sum = 10"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Output: \"\""
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Explanation:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "There are no integers that have exactly 1 digit and whose digits sum to 10. Therefore, the answer is \"\"."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Constraints:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• 1 <= num <= 2 * 10^5"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• 1 <= sum <= 2 * 10^6"
    }
  ]
}
